  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1)\nSurface cold front is currently southeast of the I-71 corridor and\nwill be exiting our remaining counties during the late afternoon \nhours. Cannot rule out an isolated shower/storm bubbling up along and\neven behind the front, but chances remain very low.\n\nBehind the frontal passage, river valley fog is expected to develop\novernight.\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2)\nA broad H5 ridge will build across a large portion of the eastern \nand central CONUS late this weekend and is expected to persist\nthrough at least the middle of next week. This feature will result in\nan influx of hot and humid air, with daytime highs returning to the\n90s for multiple days next week. Forecast looks to remain mostly dry\nthrough the early part of next week before some rain chances return\nmidweek.",
